# slug: ch28-out-of-ssa
# source: chapters/ch28.tex:124 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Out-of-SSA translation with edge splitting
# label: alg:ch28-out-of-ssa
# require: SSA function with phi nodes, CFG G
# ensure: equivalent function with no phi nodes
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE SSA function with phi nodes, CFG G
ENSURE equivalent function with no phi nodes
FORALL critical edge e that needs a phi copy DO
  split e with a fresh block S[e]
END FOR
FORALL block J with phi nodes DO
  FORALL predecessor P of J DO
    build parallel copy C[P] mapping each phi input from P to its result
    place C[P] on edge P -> J: before P's terminator if it has one successor, otherwise at J's entry if it has one predecessor, or in the split block
  END FOR
  delete the phi nodes in J
END FOR
sequence each parallel copy with temporaries for swaps
run dead-code elimination on orphaned copies

